From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] SPARC64: leave no active package after preopening /memory

preopen ends with "/chosen" as the active package, and nothing selects
another one afterwards, so the ok prompt and every client program start
with /chosen active: get-current is the /chosen node's method list and
the search order holds it in front of forth.

Solaris 10 defines its Forth words through the client interface
"interpret" (kmem64-tte, the hme hash constants, unix-tte) and later
calls "' unix-tte is va>tte-data". In between it creates its os-io
node with find-device ... device-end, which leaves the search order at
forth alone, so unix-tte, defined in /chosen, was not found:

  unix-tte:interpret: exception -13 caught
  interpret ' unix-tte is va>tte-data failed with error ffffffffffffffed

and the firmware kept translating kernel addresses with the early
kmem64-tte handler.

End preopen with device-end, as OBP leaves no package active at the ok
prompt.
---
 arch/sparc64/init.fs | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/sparc64/init.fs b/arch/sparc64/init.fs
index eb6c9da..2ffcf5a 100644
--- a/arch/sparc64/init.fs
+++ b/arch/sparc64/init.fs
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ active-package!
   else
     2drop
   then
+  device-end
 ;
 
 :noname
